// BT-3916 (ADR 0133): a user class that `uses:` the stdlib's `Enumerable` but
// defines its own `anySatisfy:` (the class wins over the provision, ADR 0127
// §3) with different semantics: it looks only at the first element. The
// stdlib provisions still thread a writing block; the class's own method is
// refused. Driven by adr0133enumerable_user_test.bt.

Value subclass: Adr0133EnumerableStdlibOwnAny
  uses: Enumerable(Integer)
  field: items :: List(Integer) = #()

  elements -> List(Integer) => self.items

  anySatisfy: block =>
    self.items isEmpty ifTrue: [^false]
    block value: self.items first
